    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d414">

                <pb facs="0681" n="577" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg577"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.654/63: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy (Garrett) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-02-23T11:00:00+01:00">February 23,
                            1933—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 23—8:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7. Your instruction No. 816, December 14, 1932. Suvich<anchor n="7"
                        xml:id="d414-f1"/> told me yesterday that some differences of opinion with
                    other Ministries still existed but he hoped to be able to take up the proposal
                    for a treaty with <pb facs="0682" n="578" xml:id="pg578"/> me on Tuesday. I
                    could not get him to commit himself further. However, in view of shortness of
                    time, I respectfully request that you send me, by the next pouch, full powers to
                    sign if and when our text is accepted or complete agreement with us reached. If
                    it cannot be signed before my departure the full powers can be returned.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d414-f1" n="7" xml:id="d414-f1-content">
                <p>Fulvio Suvich, Italian Under Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
